<title>INDIA: Indian castor prices ease on weak export interest.</title>
<headline>Indian castor prices ease on weak export interest.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian castor prices on Wednesday eased by seven rupees to 1,114/1,115 rupees on renewed speculative offerings and weak export interest, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said old crop inflows also triggered liquidation.</p>
<p>Groundnut oil fell to 388/390 rupees per 10 kg from 395/397 rupees on higher new crop arrivals and limited seasonal buying.</p>
<p>In Rajkot spot oil rose by five rupees to 550 rupees per 15 kg.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
